column59:
Lowland wet forest[200
]. Dry to very dry, or wet tropical forests[303
]. Common in more open forests, mostly on well-drained, often gravelly soils on the upper slopes of low hills and ridges

Widespread in the wet forests of tropical America, it is frequently found in upland forests and in old open woodlands[303
]. In Peru, it is common on the savannah margins[303
]. It prefers open forests with abundant light[303
].
